<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Austria</h1><p class="st-meta">1156 CE – 1453 CE · capital Vienna</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Babenberg and Habsburg duchy on the Danube, created by the Privilegium Minus in 1156, which became the core of the Habsburg monarchy.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1156 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a> issued the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/privilegium-minus">Privilegium Minus</a>, raising the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/margraviate-of-austria">Margraviate of Austria</a> to a duchy for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-duke-of-austria">Henry II Jasomirgott</a>, in compensation for giving up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>. The new duchy received special privileges, including inheritance through female lines. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> became the ducal capital.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-babenberg">Babenbergs</a> acquired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a> in 1192 and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/minnesang">Minnesang</a>. After the line died out in 1246, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottokar-ii-of-bohemia">Ottokar II of Bohemia</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, but in 1278 Rudolf I of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a> defeated him at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-on-the-marchfeld">Marchfeld</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolf-iv-duke-of-austria">Rudolf IV</a> founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/university-of-vienna">University of Vienna</a> in 1365 and forged the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/privilegium-maius">Privilegium Maius</a> to claim higher rank.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1453 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-iii-holy-roman-emperor">Emperor Frederick III</a>, himself a <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-habsburg">Habsburg</a>, confirmed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/privilegium-maius">Privilegium Maius</a>, raising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> to an archduchy. The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/archduchy-of-austria">Archduchy of Austria</a> became the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a> and, ultimately, the modern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/first-austrian-republic">Republic of Austria</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/duchy-of-austria.jpg" alt="Duchy of Austria" width="320" height="235"><figcaption>Image: Alphathon /ˈæɫfə.θɒn/ (talk) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duchy_of_Austria_locator_map_(1250).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1156 CE – 1453 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vienna</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Leopold VI of Austria, Rudolf IV of Austria, Albert II of Austria</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bavarian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Herzogtum Österreich</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1304&amp;focus=duchy-of-austria" aria-label="Duchy of Austria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5061 491 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Austria lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5381 747L5356 747M5381 747L5229 694M5381 747L5330 692M5381 747L5381 747M5381 747L5342 793M5381 747L5362 781M5381 747L5336 795M5381 747L5343 812M5381 747L5267 775"/><path class="m